From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:44:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Tell "do this" from "go there" in instruction steps (issue 6)

`kind: "action"` lived in screen metadata and never reached the output, so
an app could not tell an action step from a navigation step, or word a step
without looking the screen up again.

- InstructionStep gains `kind` ("navigate" | "action"), `actionNode` (the
  node id, action steps only) and `toName` (arrival display name).
- The fields are optional in the type so hand built steps and older
  consumers keep working; the builder always sets kind and toName.
- A step into an action node is the "action" step and carries the actions
  (issue 4). The step back out is "navigate".
- Exports the StepKind type. Tests, README, llms.txt, AGENTS.md and
  CHANGELOG updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
